          <h3 class="card-title-2 mb-4">Multicast Feeds</h3>
          <p class="body-copy mb-8">
            Raw and normalized low-latency multicast feeds covering US equities, options, and futures, plus European venues via Eurex and Euronext. The normalized format reduces bandwidth while preserving the data integrity institutional workflows require.
          </p>
          <a href="stocks-options-futures/" class="arrow-link mt-auto">Exchange feeds &amp; coverage <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="card bg-white">
          <h3 class="card-title-2 mb-4">Live APIs</h3>
          <p class="body-copy mb-8">
            API access to live market data and analytics for single stocks, ETFs, options, and futures. SpiderStream over MLink provides WebSocket and REST access to real-time and delayed institutional-grade data.
          </p>
          <a href="spiderstream-market-data-api/" class="arrow-link mt-auto">SpiderStream / MLink API <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="card bg-white">
          <h3 class="card-title-2 mb-4">Historical Datasets</h3>
          <p class="body-copy mb-8">
            10+ years of end-of-day and intraday history &mdash; options pricing, Greeks, implied volatility, and equity prices &mdash; delivered as Parquet files on AWS S3 or queried in place through Snowflake for backtesting and research.
          </p>
          <a href="historical-data-analytics/options-greeks-stock-prices/" class="arrow-link mt-auto">Historical data products <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="card bg-white">
          <h3 class="card-title-2 mb-4">AWS &amp; Infrastructure</h3>
          <p class="body-copy mb-8">
            Historical data as Parquet files on AWS S3, or queried in place through a Snowflake reader account &mdash; using the tools your team already runs.
          </p>
          <a href="aws-infrastructure/" class="arrow-link mt-auto">AWS &amp; Snowflake delivery <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

